{"name":"Espresso Martini","hex":"#8c3a00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espresso","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concentrated coffee beverage brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee.","A drink that includes espresso as an ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espresso"},{"term":"martini","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Martin (attributive); used in taxonomic names for organisms having English names of the form \"Martin's ...\""]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cocktail made with gin or vodka and vermouth.","Any cocktail served in a cocktail glass, often sweet or fruity and aimed at women."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/martini"}],"entries":[{"title":"Espresso martini","blocks":[{"text":"The espresso martini, also known as a vodka espresso, is a cold caffeinated alcoholic drink made with espresso, coffee liqueur, and vodka, served in a martini glass. It is not a true martini as it contains neither gin nor vermouth, but is one of many drinks that incorporate the term martini into their names."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Bistrot_Bruno_Loubet%2C_Clerkenwell%2C_London_%284574785649%29.jpg/330px-Bistrot_Bruno_Loubet%2C_Clerkenwell%2C_London_%284574785649%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso_martini"},{"title":"Martini (cocktail)","blocks":[{"text":"The martini is a cocktail made with gin and vermouth, garnished with an olive, a lemon twist, or both. Over the years, the martini has become one of the best-known mixed alcoholic beverages worldwide. A common variation, the vodka martini, uses vodka instead of gin for the cocktail's base spirit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0084.jpg/330px-15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0084.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martini_(cocktail)"},{"title":"Espresso","blocks":[{"text":"Espresso is a concentrated form of coffee produced by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee beans. Originating in Italy, espresso has become one of the most popular coffee-brewing methods worldwide. It is characterized by its small serving size, typically 25–30 ml, and its distinctive layers: a dark body topped with a lighter-colored foam called \"crema\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg/330px-Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/1280px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man pulls an espresso while leaning out of a train in a 1922 advertisement for a \"caffé espresso\" machine. The imagery references the shared associations of speed and steam, as well as name: in Italy, a class of trains is called \"espresso\".[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVictoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg/330px-Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"h